<title>FINLAND: FINNISH FIRMS IN DOMESTIC ROAD SHOW IN APRIL.</title>
<headline>FINNISH FIRMS IN DOMESTIC ROAD SHOW IN APRIL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourteen listed companies are scheduled to present themselves for domestic investors during a domestic road show in April, the Finnish Foundation for Share Promotion said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>The foundation will stage, together with local chambers of commerce and the ministry of trade and industry, a total of 15 events in nine different cities between April 9 and 29. Each event will feature 3-4 companies.</p>
<p>The companies participating in the road shows are:</p>
<p>Aamulehti-Yhtyma , Asko , Enso , Espoon Sahko , KCI Konecranes International , Lassila &amp; Tikanoja , Metra , Neste , Outokumpu , Partek , Raision Yhtyma , Rauma , Tamfelt and Tamrock .</p>
<p>The dates and venues are: April 9 -- Turku, April 10 -- Tampere, April 14 -- Helsinki, Pori, April 15 -- Helsinki, April 16 -- Lahti, April 17 -- Helsingfors, Vaasa, April 21 -- Helsinki, April 22 -- Espoo, April 23 -- Helsinki, April 24 -- Oulu, April 28 -- Turku, Mariehamn, April 29 -- Tampere. --Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
